file=Legal & Compliance/scribe/operational/agent/scribe-config.md · h=agent: scribe\ndepartment: Legal & Compliance\ntype: config\npurpose: >\nPlaybook, escalation, and house style. Read by contract-review-routing to\nbind YVON's config layer to the vendor-agreement-review marketplace skill\nper playbook §7 and §4.8. Field list derived from actual skill references —\nevery field in this file traces to a line in one of scribe's SKILL.md files.\nrequired_by:\n- custom/contract-review-routing/SKILL.md   # Step 2 checks for these sections by name\n- marketplace/vendor-agreement-review/SKILL.md   # via the wrapper\nconfig_debt_announcement: >\nEvery <FILL_IN> in this file is a config debt announced on every skill\ninvocation (playbook §14.7). Fill the value or mark it `n/a` with a one-line\nreason. Do not ship this agent with silent placeholders.\nlast_updated: 2026-07-29\n · s·c:scribe \· config=> **HOW TO USE.** Fill in each `<FILL_IN>` with a real value or replace it with `n/a — <one-line reason>`. Every unfilled field is announced on every skill invocation per playbook §14.7. Section headings are contract with `contract-review-routing` — do not rename them.\n\n · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Role of the operator \| `<FILL_IN — one of: lawyer / paralegal / non-lawyer>` \| · tb=\| Contact for legal escalations \| `<FILL_IN — name or role>` \| · wut:Who's using this=Non-lawyer role triggers additional bounce gates in `vendor-agreement-review` (Steps 5 and Integration/DocuSign) before redlines leave or a signature envelope is generated.\n\n · p·s:Playbook \· Sales-side=Positions used when the counterparty is a customer buying from this organisation. The eight categories match the SMB 8-category schema used by `contract-library` for template classification.\n · ### 1. Payment & cash flow=- Standard position: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker in this category: `<FILL_IN — yes/no; if yes, describe>`\n · ### 2. Liability & indemnification=- Standard position (direct cap): `<FILL_IN — e.g., "12 months fees paid">`\n- Standard position (indirect / consequential): `<FILL_IN — e.g., "excluded">`\n- Standard position (cap-carveouts): `<FILL_IN — e.g., "data breach, IP, confidentiality">`\n- Standard position (cap base): `<FILL_IN — exact wording, per marketplace skill Step 3.3>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 3. Termination & exit=- Standard position: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 4. Intellectual property=- Standard position: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 5. Scope & change management=- Standard position: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 6. Non-compete & exclusivity=- Standard position: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 7. Confidentiality & data=- Standard position (scope): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (duration): `<FILL_IN — e.g., "3 years">`\n- Standard position (DPA reference): `<FILL_IN — required / optional / n/a>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 8. Operational=- Standard position (auto-renewal): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (assignment): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (MFN): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (audit rights): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (dispute resolution): `<FILL_IN — e.g., "AAA arbitration, seat = <city>">`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n\n · p·p:Playbook \· Purchasing-side=Positions used when the counterparty is a vendor supplying this organisation. Same eight categories as above.\n · ### 1. Payment & cash flow=- Standard position: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 2. Liability & indemnification=- Standard position (direct cap): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (indirect / consequential): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (cap-carveouts): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (cap base): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 3. Termination & exit=- Standard position: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 4. Intellectual property=- Standard position: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 5. Scope & change management=- Standard position: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 6. Non-compete & exclusivity=- Standard position: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 7. Confidentiality & data=- Standard position (scope): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (duration): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (DPA required): `<FILL_IN — yes/no; if yes, house DPA template slug from contract-library>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n · ### 8. Operational=- Standard position (auto-renewal): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (assignment): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (MFN): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (audit rights): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Standard position (dispute resolution): `<FILL_IN>`\n- Acceptable fallback: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Never accept: `<FILL_IN>`\n- Deal-breaker: `<FILL_IN>`\n\n · em:Escalation matrix=Contract value + issue severity → approver. Thresholds and approver names must be real; the marketplace skill's Step 5 quality-gate rejects `"escalate to legal"` as a name.\n · tb=\| Level \| Threshold \| Approver \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| L1 \| contract value ≤ `<FILL_IN $X>` AND no 🔴 issues \| `<FILL_IN — role or named person>` \| Standard; scribe handles routing without external sign-off \| · tb=\| L2 \| `<FILL_IN $X>` < contract value ≤ `<FILL_IN $Y>` OR ≥1 🟠 issue \| `<FILL_IN — role or named person>` \| Business-unit or GC review \| · tb=\| L3 \| contract value > `<FILL_IN $Y>` OR ≥1 🔴 issue OR IP assignment OR unlimited liability \| `Governance/board` \| Fixed — constitutional threshold per department boundary ruling \| · em:Escalation matrix=Automatic-escalation triggers (any → L3 regardless of value):\n\n- Unlimited liability accepted anywhere in the memo.\n- IP assignment (broad or ambiguous scope).\n- Deal-breaker present per the list below.\n- Contract requires waiver of scribe's default confidentiality position (Section 7 above).\n\n · dl:Deal-breaker list=Terms that halt detailed review and require operator/board decision before proceeding.\n\n- `<FILL_IN — deal-breaker #1, or write "None declared — no term will halt review">`\n- `<FILL_IN — deal-breaker #2 if any>`\n- `<FILL_IN — deal-breaker #3 if any>`\n\n**The one to check first** (per marketplace skill Step 2): `<FILL_IN — pick one deal-breaker from the list above; this is the single check that runs before any term-by-term comparison>`\n\n · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Preferred governing law \| `<FILL_IN — jurisdiction and body of law, e.g., "England & Wales">` \| · tb=\| Preferred venue \| `<FILL_IN — court or arbitration seat>` \| · tb=\| Choice-of-law fallback \| `<FILL_IN — jurisdictions we will accept without escalation>` \| · tb=\| Choice-of-law never-accept \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · gl:Governing law=The marketplace skill's Step 3 jurisdiction delta check compares the contract's governing law against the top divergences (non-solicits, auto-renewal, liability exclusions, indemnification, confidentiality term). Delta findings are `[jurisdiction — verify]` flags in the memo.\n\n · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Work-product header (default) \| `<FILL_IN — the exact text to prepend to every memo; e.g., "PRIVILEGED AND CONFIDENTIAL — ATTORNEY WORK PRODUCT">` \| · tb=\| Privilege circle (default distribution) \| `<FILL_IN — comma-separated roles or names>` \| · tb=\| Preferred date format \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., "YYYY-MM-DD">` \| · tb=\| Preferred citation style \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., "Bluebook", "OSCOLA", or "n/a">` \| · tb=\| Memo format default \| `<FILL_IN — full-memo / slack-summary / both>` \| · tb=\| Redline output default \| `<FILL_IN — .docx tracked-changes / markdown / both>` \| · hs:House style=Distribution rule (fixed, not `<FILL_IN>`): destination checks per marketplace skill's opening "Destination check" apply. Public channels, company-wide lists, counterparty, vendors, and clients (for work product) waive privilege; the memo header is stripped before external delivery.\n\n · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Enabled \| `<FILL_IN — ✓ / ✗ (default ✗ for in-house)>` \| · tb=\| Matters root path (if enabled) \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Cross-matter context (if enabled) \| `<FILL_IN — on / off (default off)>` \| · tb=\| Section \| Fields \| Status \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Who's using this \| 2 \| `<FILL_IN counter — auto-populated when someone runs skillgen>` \| · tb=\| Playbook \· Sales-side \| 8 categories × ~4 fields \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Playbook \· Purchasing-side \| 8 categories × ~4 fields \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Escalation matrix \| 4 thresholds + 3 approvers \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Deal-breaker list \| ≥1 entry required \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Governing law \| 4 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| House style \| 6 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Matter workspaces \| 3 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · cds:Config debt summary=Any `<FILL_IN>` remaining above is a debt announced on every invocation per playbook §14.7. Preferred steady state: 0, or explicit `n/a` on any field the operator has decided is not applicable.\n